.cursor-wrapper{ pointer-events:none; } About Us Industries Our Expertise Products ProAdapt Command Consoles ProEdge Command Consoles ProNerve Command Console Suite ProVerse H1 Pro Touch-X Series Pro Touch-Oval Series IStandee HoloMind Pro Touch-Circular Series Hydraulic Touch Transparent iStandee ProTouch Mission Control Consoles 3D-LED Sphere Featured Works Contact Us Features Text Link Text Link Text Link Text Link Use cases Professional Pricing Learn Contact About Us Industries Our Expertise Products ProAdapt Command Consoles ProEdge Command Consoles ProNerve Command Console Suite ProVerse H1 Pro Touch-X Series Pro Touch-Oval Series IStandee HoloMind Pro Touch-Circular Series Hydraulic Touch Transparent iStandee ProTouch Mission Control Consoles 3D-LED Sphere Featured Works Contact Us Leading Aerospace Engine Manufacturer, Immersive AR/VR/MR Training & Showcase Platform Highlights A transformative initiative by one of the world’s leading aerospace engine manufacturers to reimagine internal learning and client engagement using Mixed Reality (MR), Augmented Reality (AR), and Virtual Reality (VR). Pro Digital Labs designed and delivered a high-impact immersive ecosystem that translated complex engineering into interactive, intuitive experiences—enhancing employee understanding and elevating customer storytelling across touch tables, video walls, and spatial computing environments. Client A Leading Global Aerospace Engine Manufacturer Type Immersive Experience & Training Platform Sector Aerospace, Engineering & Manufacturing Scope Component-Level Storytelling for AR, VR, MR, and Interactive Display Systems The Challenge The client was grappling with the challenge of translating highly technical engine schematics into a format that could be easily understood across internal teams and external stakeholders. Traditional training methods—consisting of static CAD files, diagrams, and dense documentation—offered little interactivity and often failed to communicate the functional relationships between engine components effectively. For internal teams, this hindered training efficiency, particularly for new hires and cross-functional staff unfamiliar with the intricate mechanical details. For external customers, there was no compelling way to demonstrate the innovation embedded within each engine variant. The company needed an intelligent, scalable, and visually impactful platform that could bridge these two critical audiences: engineers seeking clarity and customers seeking confidence. Our Solution Pro Digital envisioned a cross-platform immersive storytelling system that converted the client’s raw CAD and engineering files into interactive digital experiences. Each engine component was digitally exploded and restructured into a real-time 3D environment. These virtual assemblies were then embedded with contextual narratives and visual cues to illustrate function, connectivity, and innovation. To ensure maximum accessibility and engagement, we developed a suite of applications that spanned: Mixed Reality Training Modules: Using MR headsets to simulate real-time maintenance, part identification, and troubleshooting walkthroughs. Virtual Reality Exploration: Enabling deep dives into engine internals in fully immersive environments for training and presentations. Augmented Reality Showcases: Deploying mobile-based AR to visualize components on-site or during events with animated overlays. Interactive Touch Tables & Video Walls: Allowing both one-on-one and group explorations of the engine through intuitive touch interfaces and dynamic component storytelling. We also built a custom CMS-driven backend that centralized all content, enabling real-time updates, multilingual deployment, and hardware-specific optimization across touch tables, AR/VR devices, and holographic displays. Our Scope Included Pro Digital delivered a full turnkey solution, starting from technology consulting and spatial planning to immersive content creation and system integration. We began by transforming the client's detailed CAD/engineering data into real-time 3D models using a mix of mesh optimization, texture mapping, and animation layering techniques. This engineering data was then augmented with contextual insights—such as material properties, mechanical functions, inter-component dependencies, and assembly processes—converted into micro-stories within the application interface. We developed immersive experiences across MR headsets, VR pods, and AR environments, each tailored for different use cases—training, sales, and exhibitions. Additionally, we designed custom UI/UX systems for multi-touch tables and video walls, enabling real-time interaction with component animations, callouts, and content overlays. Our team also implemented a scalable content management engine to allow remote updates and localization of content. The final deployment included hardware calibration, integration of our proprietary Pro Touch Tables and OLED-based video walls, staff training, and post-deployment technical support to ensure optimal performance and engagement. The Impact 60% Reduction in internal training time, achieved by replacing static technical documentation with interactive component-level walkthroughs. Faster Onboarding of new engineers and non-technical staff, facilitated by intuitive visual storytelling and step-by-step explorable modules. Elevated Customer Engagement: Customers gained a clearer understanding of the value proposition through immersive demos that brought the engine’s complexity to life. Cross-Platform Content Reuse: One unified content pipeline served multiple deployment channels—AR/VR/MR, touch tables, and mobile—ensuring consistency, reducing duplication, and streamlining maintenance. Why It Matters This case represents a benchmark in how emerging immersive technologies can be strategically leveraged to transform both internal learning and external communication in high-tech manufacturing sectors. By elevating engineering data into experiential narratives, Pro Digital helped the client bridge the knowledge gap between engineers and decision-makers—turning technical depth into visual clarity. As more industries embrace digital twins and simulation-led learning, this implementation stands out as a replicable model for those seeking to humanize complex innovations, improve operational readiness, and create unforgettable customer touchpoints. Read Government of Karnataka, iWorkstation Deployment for Student Hostels This is some text inside of a div block. Read Department of Mines & Geology, Karnataka: iStandee Deployment Across Districts This is some text inside of a div block. Read BBMP Hospitals, Government of Karnataka | Digital Signage Upgrade for Public Healthcare Centres This is some text inside of a div block. .white-grid {
